ies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-38\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-39\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FF\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-40\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"PL\"]},\n    {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-41\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-42\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-43\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"PL\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-44\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"PL\"]},\n    {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-45\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-46\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FIFA\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-47\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"FF\"]}, {\"cardId\":\"QB-A-48\",\"batchId\":\"GPI-005\",\"revision\":1,\"sourceFamilies\":[\"PL\"]}\n  ],\n  \"recordDefaults\": {\n    \"status\": \"draft\",\n    \"selectionEligible\": false,\n    \"originalityRecord\": {\"decision\":\"pending\",\"reasonCode\":\"ORIGINALITY-UNAUTHORED\"},\n    \"provenance\": {\"decision\":\"pending\",\"reasonCode\":\"PROVENANCE-LOCATOR-MISSING\"},\n    \"reviews\": [\n      {\"role\":\"factual_rights_editor\",\"decision\":\"pending\",\"reasonCode\":\"FACTUAL-RIGHTS-REVIEW-PENDING\"},\n      {\"role\":\"accessibility_copy_editor\",\"decision\":\"pending\",\"reasonCode\":\"ACCESSIBILITY-COPY-REVIEW-PENDING\"}\n    ],\n    \"releaseGate\": {\"decision\":\"pending\",\"reasonCode\":\"RELEASE-GATE-INCOMPLETE\"}\n  },\n  \"validation\": {\n    \"exactCardIdPattern\": \"^QB-A-(0[1-9]|[1-3][0-9]|4[0-8])$\",\n    \"expectedRecordCount\": 48,\n    \"expectedBatchCount\": 4,\n    \"expectedCardsPerBatch\": 12,\n    \"requiredPendingReasonCodes\": [\"ORIGINALITY-UNAUTHORED\",\"PROVENANCE-LOCATOR-MISSING\",\"FACTUAL-RIGHTS-REVIEW-PENDING\",\"ACCESSIBILITY-COPY-REVIEW-PENDING\",\"RELEASE-GATE-INCOMPLETE\"]\n  }\n}\n---\ntask_id: GD0003\nsequence: 6\ndependencies: GD0002\nsource_specifications: design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md,design-evidence/qba-editorial-acceptance-register.json,design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md,planning/game-design-manifest.json\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007\ntitle: Dispatch remaining bounded QB-A editorial evidence work\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nThis is the sole successor dispatcher for the unresolved QB-A editorial\nrecords recorded by `GD0002`. It preserves the existing 48-card boundary and\ndoes not create cards, publish cards, alter quiz scope, create B/R runbooks, or\naccept `../planning/game-design-manifest.json`.\n\nThe current register deliberately records all 48 revision-1 cards as `draft`\nand `selectionEligible: false`. Every card retains the exact reasons\n`ORIGINALITY-UNAUTHORED`, `PROVENANCE-LOCATOR-MISSING`,\n`FACTUAL-RIGHTS-REVIEW-PENDING`, `ACCESSIBILITY-COPY-REVIEW-PENDING`, and\n`RELEASE-GATE-INCOMPLETE`. No default, batch-level decision, or future wave\nmay substitute for a card's current-revision evidence.\n\n## Bounded editorial waves\n\nEach wave below is limited to one existing 12-card batch. Within a wave, author\nevidence first and review it only after the current-revision authoring evidence\nis complete. A card that is rejected, unresolved, conflicted, withdrawn, or\nmissing any required record stays ineligible with its exact reason retained.\n\n| Wave | Existing batch | Fixed card IDs | Required card-level work | Completion boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | `GPI-002` \u2014 World Tournament History | `QB-A-01`\u2013`QB-A-12` | Original expression; exact permitted-source locators and checked dates for every assertion; conflict/correction state; factual/rights review; accessibility/copy review; independent second review. | 12 current-revision records only. |\n| E2 | `GPI-003` \u2014 Domestic League Moments | `QB-A-13`\u2013`QB-A-24` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1. | 12 current-revision records only. |\n| E3 | `GPI-004` \u2014 Club, Manager, and Identity | `QB-A-25`\u2013`QB-A-36` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1, including both permitted source routes where stated. | 12 current-revision records only. |\n| E4 | `GPI-005` \u2014 Players and Records | `QB-A-37`\u2013`QB-A-48` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1. | 12 current-revision records only. |\n\nFor every card, the factual/rights and accessibility/copy decisions must be\naccepted by distinct reviewers for the exact revision. The release editor may\nset `published` only after those accepted decisions, accepted originality and\nprovenance evidence, no unresolved conflict, and the defined lifecycle\ntransitions. Until then a selector must reject it because the register's\nselection rule remains binding.\n\n## GQ audit gate\n\nDo not create a `GQ` audit while any of the 48 records remains un-authored,\npending, blocked, rejected, conflicted, withdrawn, or otherwise ineligible.\nOnly after all four waves contain actual accepted evidence may a later `GQ`\naudit run the dedicated completion check, update canonical bible/inventory\nrecords, and accept the manifest. This dispatcher does none of those actions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The QB-A catalogue remains exactly four existing named batches of 12 cards\n  (48 IDs total), with no replacement or added card.\n- Each still-ineligible card retains its exact reason and cannot enter\n  selection until current-revision evidence and two distinct accepted reviews\n  qualify it.\n- No `GQ` audit is created and the manifest remains pending until all 48\n  records have actual accepted evidence.\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia